A string literal missing its closing `"`. It runs to end of file, so the
statements after it are swallowed: unterminated_string on the opening
quote, and the :IF whose :ENDIF sits inside the swallowed text is still
reported by unclosed_block on its opener (diag.unterminated_string).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Greeting;
	:PARAMETERS sName;
	:DECLARE sText;
	:IF Empty(sName);
		sText := "Hello, guest;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sText;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Greeting;
	:PARAMETERS sName;
	:DECLARE sText;
	:IF Empty(sName);
		sText := "Hello, guest;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sText;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:11 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':PROCEDURE' - expected ':ENDPROC'
4:2-4:5 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
5:12-5:13 error unterminated_string: Unterminated string literal - expected a closing '"' before end of file
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:11 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':PROCEDURE' - expected ':ENDPROC'
4:2-4:5 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
5:12-5:13 error unterminated_string: Unterminated string literal - expected a closing '"' before end of file
